<title>BELGIUM: EU does not quantify fine-avoiding recession.</title>
<headline>EU does not quantify fine-avoiding recession.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has not quantified the definition of an economic condition it calls &quot;severe recession&quot; which would help EU members which have entered EMU avoid fines for running excessive deficits.</p>
<p>European Commissioner Yves-Thibault De Silguy told a news conference that a country would escape Commission fines if it went through a period of &quot;significant negative growth.&quot;</p>
<p>He gave no details, but said the circumstances in each country would have be analysed and therefore differences between countries precluded putting exact figures on what constituted a severe recession.</p>
